{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Timer names are bare strings wherever they are unambiguous. Two owners","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the game and a bundle, or two bundles) may both declare one name: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"bootstrap moves each bundle-owned declaration into its namespace"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Clock.roam\""},{"type":"text","text":") while the game’s own stays bare, and a body running for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its owner resolves the bare literal it declared against that owner first"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and friends). A host game addresses a bundle’s"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"collided timer by the qualified name."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Timers tick once per typed command, at the very end of the turn (after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the world’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":"\/each-turn rules): fuses first, then daemons, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"group in name order. They tick on refused turns (world time passes) but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not on parse errors, meta commands, or once the game has ended. A timer"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"started earlier in the turn ticks at the end of that same turn — so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fuse(after: 1)"},{"type":"text","text":" started by a rule fires as that very turn ends. A timer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"started or restarted "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"while the tick runs"}]},{"text":" — by a fuse or daemon body, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by anything a body calls — is a turn behind that: the tick skips it, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first ticks at the end of the next turn, wherever its name sorts.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"title":"TimedEvent","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TimedEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"externalID":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/timedevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"A named timed event, declared in a game or bundle ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block: a fuse","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or 